<title>UK: Amstrad shares suspended before hearing.</title>
<headline>Amstrad shares suspended before hearing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British consumer electronics group Amstrad Plc have been suspended temporarily at the company's request pending a court hearing on its restructuring, the London Stock Exchange said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Amstrad said last week the hearing would be held on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Under the reorganisation, Amstrad plans to change its name to Viglen Technology Plc. The company is expected to begin trading under the new name on August 4.</p>
<p>Amstrad's shares closed at 278-1/2p on Monday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
